मण्डलम् अर्थ ॥ ॰ artha — the port of crates/sadhana/src/t1/{resolve,typecheck,types}.rs

॰ ADR-0030 REMEDIATION, TASK `D-002h`. THE FILE TAKEN BY THIS CYCLE IS THIS ONE,
॰ THE FOURTH OF THE REPAIR after `ir.t1`, `ast.t1` and `vishlesana.t1`. All 39
॰ of its 64-bit integer positions read `अ६४` and now read `न६४`, and not one
॰ moves the other way: this file holds NO signed quantity at all. Every site is
॰ a DISCRIMINANT numbered from १, an INDEX into an arena or a scope slice, a
॰ LENGTH, a SymbolId or Ty::Int's `width`, and none of the six can be negative.
॰
॰ THE TWIN IS WHOLE HERE, WHICH IS WHY THIS FILE WAS TAKEN NEXT. `ast.t1`
॰ found the method's gap — read each site's sign off its Rust twin — where the
॰ port had run ahead of `crates/sadhana`; `vishlesana.t1` showed the gap is a
॰ property of particular files. This one settles it in the other direction:
॰ `t1/types.rs`'s `Ty` has TWELVE variants and the twelve `*अर्थभेद` constants
॰ below are those twelve, in the same order, one for one — the first file of
॰ the repair whose twin reaches EVERY kind constant it declares. `Ty::Int`'s
॰ `width: u8` and `Ty::Float`'s `width: u8` are unsigned outright;
॰ `SymbolId` is `pub struct SymbolId(pub usize)` and `Resolver::next_symbol`
॰ is `usize`. There is no `i64` and no `isize` anywhere in
॰ `t1/{types,resolve,typecheck}.rs`.
॰
॰ RE-FOUNDED 2026-09-05 (`W-274`, `W-277`), AND IT LOST A WITNESS RATHER THAN
॰ A COUNTEREXAMPLE. This read "`SymbolId` and `NodeId` are `pub usize`
॰ (`t1/ast.rs:4`, `:7`)". `NodeId` was DELETED — `pub`, constructed nowhere,
॰ and invisible to `dead_code` for exactly that reason — so the claim now
॰ rests on `SymbolId` alone. It is still true and it has half the support it
॰ had; saying so is the point, because a citation that silently loses a
॰ witness is how a true claim stops being checkable.
॰
॰ AND THE LINE NUMBERS WERE WRONG TWICE OVER: `ast.rs:4` is now `:24` and
॰ `resolve.rs:11` is now `:32`, both moved by edits ABOVE them that had
॰ nothing to do with this claim. Nothing here reads a margin's line number,
॰ so that decay is silent. Cited BY NAME above for that reason — a name
॰ survives every edit that does not delete the thing named.
॰
॰ AND FIVE OF THE 39 ARE INVISIBLE TO THE 1378 CENSUS, which counts the token
॰ immediately after `ॱॱ` or after `ददाति`. Where the type is wrapped that token
॰ is the WRAPPER: `सम्भाव्य न६४` is written four times (`परिसरान्वेषणम्` and
॰ `नामनिर्णयः` return it, `पुनरुक्तघोषणम्` and `नामनिर्णयः` bind it) and
॰ `दोषयुक्त न६४` once (`घोषणम्`), so the ledger moves by 34 while the file
॰ moves by 39. `vishlesana.t1` found the same shortfall at `अङ्कः अन्तः`; two
॰ different wrappers now hide sites from it, and the census stays a LOWER BOUND
॰ on the work rather than a measure of it.

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE SEMA — name resolution and the type checker, task D-002c, doc 03 §8
॰ phase 3.5.5. Doc 03 §2's own table names this stage:
॰
॰     अर्थ      artha     sema / typecheck / comptime  (T1)
॰
॰ ── WHY THIS FILE IS NEW AND WHAT IT TOOK OVER FROM ──
॰ The sema's T1 port existed, machine-transliterated, INSIDE विश्लेषण.त१,
॰ as मण्डलम् वइशलएसअन. That is the disassembler's file: spec/marks.tsv row
॰ `vishlesana`, spec/lexicon.src.tsv line 437 and task B-013 all name
॰ विश्लेषणम् the disassembler, and crates/sadhana/src/vishlesana.rs is 231
॰ lines of one. The sema had been written into it.
॰
॰ THAT MISFILING WAS A LIVE BLOCKER, NOT AN UNTIDINESS. संयोजन.त१'s stub
॰ note (b) says संस्कारः "needs विश्लेषण ॱ decode ... विश्लेषण is still
॰ port_encode.py output" — and no amount of finishing that file could have
॰ produced decode, because the module in it was not the disassembler. The
॰ two are now separated: the disassembler is विश्लेषण.त१ and the sema is
॰ here, and neither had to be discarded to do it.
॰
॰ ── THREE RUST FILES, ONE MODULE ──
॰ Rust splits the sema across three files that only make sense together:
॰   t1/types.rs      17 lines   enum Ty — the type lattice
॰   t1/resolve.rs   201 lines   Resolver — scopes and names
॰   t1/typecheck.rs 175 lines   TypeChecker — types over the AST
॰ They are one मण्डलम् here because T1 has no submodules and because
॰ typecheck.rs cannot be read without Ty or without Resolver.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAME वास्तु, WHICH IS AMBIGUOUS IN THIS CRATE TODAY ──
॰ This file needs the T1 AST — अभिव्यञ्जक, वाक्य, प्रकार. Those live in
॰ अस्त.त१ (ast.t1), which declares मण्डलम् वास्तु. So does the intended
॰ hand-port of वस्तु.त१ (vastu.t1), the OBJECT READER, which संयोजन already
॰ names as वास्तुॱवस्तु. TWO DIFFERENT MODULES ARE CLAIMING वास्तु. That is
॰ not this row's to settle and it is not settled here: the import below is
॰ written, the collision is recorded, and whoever hand-ports वस्तु.त१ must
॰ resolve it. Recording it is worth more than picking a side quietly, since
॰ nothing in the tree resolves imports yet and so nothing would complain.
॰
॰ ── THE MISFILING HAD ALREADY SPREAD TO A THIRD FILE ──
॰ मध्य.त१ (ir.t1), hand-ported hours before this file existed, says of its
॰ own SymbolId placeholder: "विश्लेषण is that resolver and is D-002c; when
॰ it lands this line is one lookup, not a redesign." Its author read the
॰ misfiled विश्लेषण.त१ and drew the only conclusion its contents supported.
॰ THE SENTENCE IS NOW WRONG IN ONE WORD AND RIGHT IN EVERYTHING ELSE: the
॰ resolver is अर्थ, this file, and नामनिर्णयः below is the lookup it means.
॰ It is not edited from here — मध्य.त१ is another row's file and had just
॰ landed — but it is recorded so the correction is a word and not an
॰ excavation. That a second worker built on the wrong premise within hours
॰ is the measure of what a misfiled module costs.
॰
॰ ── ON GROUPING ── every order-dependent expression is bracketed with
॰ आरभ्य ॱ समाप्तम्. spec/grammar-t1.ebnf freezes the three phrase constructs
॰ and says OPERATORS AND THEIR PRECEDENCE ARE NOT FROZEN; both readings
॰ already exist in this crate. संयोजन and विश्लेषण bracket for the same
॰ reason.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS NOT PORTED, AND WHY ── see the stubs at the foot of the file.
॰ Each returns अपूर्णम् and names the thing it waits on. They fall into
॰ exactly two groups and both are stated there in full.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

॰ IMPORTED DELIBERATELY 2026-09-01, WHICH IS WHAT BLOCKER (c) ASKED FOR.
॰
॰ (c) says the two arms that need name text are "one import of पदविभाग away —
॰ and that import is a decision about which मण्डलम् the sema depends on, which
॰ is worth taking deliberately rather than as a side effect of this row." It is
॰ taken here, on its own line, with the reason written down.
॰
॰ THE PRECEDENT IS 4-0 AND NOT A NEW DIRECTION: encode.t1, ir.t1, parse.t1 and
॰ vakyavibhaga.t1 all import पदविभाग already. The sema is the fifth consumer of
॰ the token store, not the first, so this settles no question the crate had not
॰ already settled four times.
॰
॰ WHAT IT BUYS: वास्तु ॱ अभिव्यञ्जक ॱ मूल्यसूचकाङ्क and वास्तु ॱ प्रकार ॱ
॰ नामसूचकाङ्क are TOKEN INDICES, not text — मध्य.त१ says so at अङ्कमूल्यम्.
॰ The text lives in पदविभाग ॱ चिह्नककोश, so the Identifier arm of
॰ अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः can now recover the नाम ॱॱ पाठ that नामनिर्णयः takes, and
॰ the Primitive arm of प्रकारार्थः the one मूलप्रकारार्थः takes.
॰
॰ WHAT IT DOES NOT BUY: blocker (d), the अर्थप्रकार arena, is untouched. That
॰ one is about OWNERSHIP rather than capability — the file's own words — and an
॰ import does not answer who owns an arena.
आयातः पदविभाग ।
॰ IMPORTED DELIBERATELY 2026-09-01, AND IT IS WHAT BLOCKER (b) REDUCED TO.
॰
॰ (b) read "THE AST HAS NO DECLARATION AND NO PROGRAM … व्याकर.त१ DOES declare
॰ घोषणा and घोषणाकोश, so the declarations exist — in another मण्डलम् this file
॰ does not import." Its own amendment then moved it to (c): व्याकर lexes now,
॰ so घोषणाकोश is reachable, "but घोषणा ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क is a TOKEN INDEX and
॰ घोषणम् takes a नाम ॱॱ पाठ". (c) IS DISCHARGED — पदविभाग is imported above —
