आयातः व्याकर ।
आयातः वास्तु ।

॰ ॥ THE SHARED DECLARATION STORE ॥ W-223 part 2, 2026-09-04. A qualified use
॰ names a member of ANOTHER module, and this pass sees one program: until the
॰ store existed the member was "taken on trust" and no symbol was written for
॰ it. `घोषणासञ्चय` holds what every collected module declares, so the member can
॰ be looked up by name. Its authority is PER MODULE and not per store — see
॰ `असदस्यमस्ति` below.
आयातः घोषणासञ्चय ।


॰ ══════════════════ the type lattice — t1/types.rs ══════════════════
॰
॰ Rust writes Ty as a twelve-variant enum with three of the variants
॰ carrying a Box<Ty> and three carrying a SymbolId. T1 has no Box and no
॰ payload-carrying गणना, so the discriminant is an integer constant and the
॰ payloads are fields that only some भेद use — the same flattening अस्त.त१
॰ already applies to अभिव्यञ्जक and प्रकार, and for the same reason.

॰ THE SEPARATING SPACE, AT MODULE SCOPE. `विवरम्` is ADR-0018's word for
॰ U+0020 and lexes as a layout WORD, not an identifier, so `विवरम् अङ्कः ० अन्तः`
॰ resolves at module scope and is REFUSED inside a routine body — which is where
॰ W-248 first wrote it, copied from `utsarjana.t1:791` where it already sits out
॰ here for the same reason. NAMED APART FROM utsarjana's `विवराष्टकम्` ON PURPOSE:
॰ globals are one flat key, so hoisting under the same spelling made a NINTH
॰ two-module collision and `t1_modules`'s load-order ratchet caught it — the very
॰ class W-249 demonstrated hours earlier. Main was red on the hoisting ratchet for exactly this
॰ (2026-09-05, `undeclared विवरम् at line 611`), and the ratchet is `#[ignore]`d,
॰ so a whole-crate run does not reach it — only `tools/light-gate.sh` does.
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारपाठविवराष्टकम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति विवरम् अङ्कः ० अन्तः ।

सार्वजनिक चरः पूर्णाङ्कार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।     ॰ Ty::Int { width, signed }
सार्वजनिक चरः प्लवार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।       ॰ Ty::Float { width }
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।       ॰ Ty::Pointer
सार्वजनिक चरः खण्डार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।        ॰ Ty::Slice
सार्वजनिक चरः सम्भाव्यार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।     ॰ Ty::Optional
सार्वजनिक चरः दोषयुक्तार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।     ॰ Ty::ErrorUnion
सार्वजनिक चरः संरचनार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ ।       ॰ Ty::Struct(SymbolId)
सार्वजनिक चरः संघार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ८ ।         ॰ Ty::Union(SymbolId)
सार्वजनिक चरः गणनार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९ ।         ॰ Ty::Enum(SymbolId)
सार्वजनिक चरः शून्यार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १० ।       ॰ Ty::Void
सार्वजनिक चरः अभावार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ११ ।       ॰ Ty::Never
सार्वजनिक चरः दोषार्थभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १२ ।        ॰ Ty::Error — poison, for recovery

॰ `W-248` — THE SPELLING THE TEXT READER MET AND DOES NOT KNOW, kept rather
॰ than counted alone: a count says how often and a name says which, and the
॰ repair needs the which. Same shape as `अनिर्णीत…` above.
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारपाठमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारपाठ ॱॱ पाठ भवति आरभ्य उक्तम् इति समाप्तम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारपाठसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ AND THE RUN, not only the last one. A single slot answers "how often" and
॰ "which one last", and the repair needs EVERY spelling — this row was opened
॰ partly because the checker's own untypable record is first-only, so 4 were
॰ counted and 2 named. Writing the same shape here would repeat the defect
॰ inside its own fix. Appender shape: advance, then write.
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारपाठकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः पाठ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारपाठसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ AND WHY, NOT ONLY WHICH ॥ `W-265`, 2026-09-05.
॰
॰ `W-248` kept the SPELLING and that was the whole record: every refusal read
॰ "this reader does not know this text", which is one sentence for five
॰ different situations and tells a repairer nothing about which one it met. A
॰ bare name nobody declares, a bare name TWO modules declare, a qualified name
॰ whose module is not in the store, a qualified name whose module has no such
॰ type, and an EMPTY spelling are five distinct facts about the program and
॰ about the store, and only the last four are actionable at all.
॰
॰ THE FAILURE MODE THIS AREA HAS IS SILENCE, and a reason that says "unknown"
॰ is silence with a number attached. `पाठः` was matched only in its RETIRED
॰ spelling for five days and every `ददाति पाठ` in the corpus read as poison
॰ while the pass reported success — found the day `W-248` made the refusal name
॰ the spelling. The reason is the same instrument one turn further on.
सार्वजनिक चरः अनामप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।     ॰ bare; no module binds this spelling
सार्वजनिक चरः असञ्चितप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।   ॰ the module is known and declares no such type
सार्वजनिक चरः रिक्तप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।     ॰ an empty spelling — there is no name to resolve
सार्वजनिक चरः बहुमण्डलप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।  ॰ bare; MORE THAN ONE module declares it
सार्वजनिक चरः अमण्डलप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।    ॰ `मण्डलॱनाम` whose मण्डल the store does not hold

सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।    ॰ the LAST refusal's reason
सार्वजनिक चरः अज्ञातप्रकारकारणकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।  ॰ and the run, beside the spellings

॰ ॥ THE SYMBOL A TYPE NAME DENOTES ॥ `W-265`, 2026-09-05.
॰
॰ `अर्थप्रकार` has carried a `संज्ञा` field since it was written — Rust's
॰ `Ty::Struct(SymbolId)`, `Ty::Union(SymbolId)`, `Ty::Enum(SymbolId)` — and
॰ NOTHING FILLED IT. Neither path from a source to a type could turn a type
॰ NAME into a SYMBOL, so a routine declared `ददाति अर्थप्रकार` typed as poison
॰ on the AST side and as poison on the text side, for the same missing reason.
॰
॰ FOUR PARALLEL DENSE RUNS AND A CURSOR, which is this corpus's own shape for a
॰ keyed table (`सञ्चयसंज्ञाप्रविष्टयः`/`सञ्चयसंज्ञामूल्यानि` below, and that
॰ record's margin says why two dense runs and not one sparse one). Slot ० is
॰ reserved; advance, then write.
॰   ॱ `प्रकारसंज्ञानामानि` — the spelling, exactly as it was written
॰   ॱ `प्रकारसंज्ञामण्डलानि` — WHOSE type it is: a `घोषणासञ्चय` module index, or
॰     ० for a type THIS program declares. A bare spelling means "this module's"
॰     and the store keeps every module's texts in the source's own spelling, so
॰     a spelling alone is not a key — `आज्ञा` is declared by `मध्यरूप` AND by
॰     `वाक्यविभाग`, and a table keyed on the text alone would answer one of them
॰     and never say which.
॰   ॱ `प्रकारसंज्ञाभेदाः` — the `अर्थप्रकार ॱ भेद` it denotes: `संरचनार्थभेद` for
॰     a `संरचना`, `गणनार्थभेद` for a `गणना`. Read off `व्याकर`'s own declaration
॰     kind, not guessed here.
॰   ॱ `प्रकारसंज्ञामूल्यानि` — SymbolId+१, the same keying `संज्ञाप्रकारकोश`,
॰     `संज्ञाभेदकोश` and `वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जक ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क` all use, so ० stays
॰     "none" and a reader needs no second convention.
॰
॰ CLEARED BY `निर्णायकारम्भः`, and that is forced rather than chosen: a symbol
॰ comes from `निर्णायकः ॱ अग्रिमसंज्ञा`, which restarts with every resolver, so a
॰ binding held over names a DIFFERENT symbol in the next resolver's numbering.
॰ The rule this file already states — an arena keyed by a numbering is cleared
॰ wherever that numbering restarts — applies here unchanged.
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारसंज्ञानामानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः पाठ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारसंज्ञामण्डलानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारसंज्ञाभेदाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारसंज्ञामूल्यानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रकारसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ THE WEAKER RULE, COUNTED RATHER THAN SILENT ॥ A BARE spelling read with no
॰ module — which is every spelling a caller hands `प्रकारपाठार्थः` directly —
॰ resolves against THIS program's declarations first. When the program declares
॰ no such type the reader falls back to "exactly one collected module declares
॰ this spelling", which is the only sound reading a bare text admits, and is
॰ WEAKER than a module-keyed lookup because it depends on what was collected.
॰ Two modules declaring it is `बहुमण्डलप्रकारकारण` and is refused, never picked
॰ between. This counter says how often the weak rule carried an answer; a
॰ reader who wants the strong one reads the number and knows.
॰ AND THE SPELLINGS, not only the count — this row's own thesis applied to its
॰ own instrument. A count says the weak rule carried 23 answers and a run says
॰ WHICH 23, and only the second can be read for whether any of them is wrong.
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्यमण्डलप्रकारसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ THE COUNT IS PER RESOLVER AND THE RUN IS PER IMAGE, deliberately and not by
॰ oversight. `निर्णायकारम्भः` zeroes the count because a census SUMS it per
॰ source and a counter that does not restart while the thing it counts does is
॰ a triangular over-count (`W-249`'s family). The RUN is not cleared, so a
॰ reader of one image sees every spelling the weak rule carried across all of
॰ it, which is what a reader wants from a list of names.
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्यमण्डलप्रकारकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः पाठ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्यमण्डलप्रकारसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ A STORE ENTRY WITH NO TYPE TEXT ॥ `W-265`. `अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या` counts a
॰ member whose RETURN could not be recorded, and an entry that declares no type
॰ at all — a `संरचना`, a `गणना`, a `वृत्ति` with no `ददाति` — has no return to
॰ fail at. Counting those there made one number out of two facts. They are
॰ counted here instead, and the two sum to what the one used to hold.
सार्वजनिक चरः रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ one type — Ty.
सार्वजनिक संरचना अर्थप्रकार आरभ्य
  भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                ॰ which variant — Ty's discriminant, numbered from १
  विस्तार ॱॱ न६४ ऽ            ॰ Ty::Int/Ty::Float's `width: u8`; ० otherwise
  चिह्नितम् ॱॱ बूल ऽ           ॰ signed, for Int; असत्यम् otherwise
  संज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ ऽ              ॰ the SymbolId(pub usize) of Struct, Union, Enum; ० else
  अन्तःसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४         ॰ the Box<Ty> of Pointer, Slice, Optional and ErrorUnion,
समाप्तम् ।                     ॰ as an index into अर्थप्रकारकोश below — usize

॰ BLOCKER (d) DECIDED: `अन्तःसूचकाङ्क` above was written to index "a caller's
॰ प्रकार arena" because none existed, and two sites (`मूलप्रकारार्थः`'s
॰ `अक्षरम्`/`पाठः`, `प्रकारार्थः`'s string-literal arm) stayed poison or wrote a
॰ placeholder ० rather than choose one. LIVES HERE, NOT IN `अस्त.त१`: the
॰ earlier note assumed it belonged beside `अभिव्यञ्जककोश`/`वाक्यकोश` because
॰ those are the corpus's only other arenas, but `अर्थप्रकार` is a TYPE, not an
॰ AST node — `अस्त.त१` is imported BY this file and imports nothing itself, so
॰ putting a type arena there would need a cycle for no reason. It belongs with
॰ its only producer and only consumer, which is `अर्थ`.
॰
॰ SLOT ० RESERVED, ADVANCE-THEN-WRITE, exactly this corpus's other arenas.
सार्वजनिक चरः अर्थप्रकारसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० । ॰ next free index into अर्थप्रकारकोश
सार्वजनिक चरः अर्थप्रकारकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अर्थप्रकार भवति ० ।

॰ push one अर्थप्रकार, answer its slot — the appender the arena above needed.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः अर्थप्रकारयोजनम् आदाय प्रकार ॱॱ अर्थप्रकार ददाति न६४ आदि
    अर्थप्रकारसूचकाङ्क भवति अर्थप्रकारसूचकाङ्क योगः १ ।
    अर्थप्रकारकोश अङ्कः अर्थप्रकारसूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति प्रकार ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् अर्थप्रकारसूचकाङ्क ।
