सार्वजनिक चरः असत्क्षेत्रमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः असत्क्षेत्रनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।     ॰ the field asked for
सार्वजनिक चरः असत्क्षेत्रवस्तु ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।    ॰ the struct that lacks it
सार्वजनिक चरः असत्क्षेत्रपङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ A STRUCT WHOSE FIELD LIST THE REGISTRY DOES NOT HOLD ॥ (2026-09-22)
॰ The cross-module walk answered the poison in SILENCE when it found no field
॰ of that name: no count, no site, and `ir.t1` then planted a stub (cause ३९).
॰ The two cases want opposite fixes and so are counted apart — a field the
॰ registry KNOWS the struct lacks is the program's defect, while an EMPTY field
॰ list is `घोषणासञ्चय`'s, and blaming the program for it would send a reader to
॰ the wrong file.
सार्वजनिक चरः असञ्चितक्षेत्रसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ `ऋण` ON SOMETHING THAT IS NOT A NUMBER ॥ (2026-09-23)
सार्वजनिक चरः अऋण्यसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ ॥ A FIELD READ WHOSE RECORD CANNOT BE RESOLVED ॥ (2026-09-23)
॰ The field arm had FOUR exits that answered the poison in SILENCE before the
॰ walks even began: the base does not type as a record (१), the record type
॰ carries no symbol (२), the symbol table is shorter than that symbol (३), and
॰ the collected registry holds no entry for it (४). A field read that took any
॰ of them COMPILED — measured 2026-09-23, `क ॱ क्षेत्रम्` on an `अ६४` emitted an
॰ object — and `ir.t1` then planted a stub for it.
॰ NONE OF THE FOUR REFUSES, AND THE MEASUREMENT THAT SAYS SO TOOK THREE TRIES.
॰ A first version refused all four, on a census through `t1_boot` that read ZERO
॰ firings over the 21 sources. `t1_boot` LOADS THE WHOLE SOURCE DIRECTORY before
॰ compiling. `t1_corpus_conditionals` and `t1_corpus_globals` compile each source
॰ ALONE, and there the exits are ordinary: 13 sources stopped emitting objects.
॰ Restricting to exit १ did not save it. Those 13 all read base kind १२
॰ (`दोषार्थभेद`) — a poison this routine returns when it has ALREADY failed
॰ upstream, so the refusal named where the poison was next read, not the defect.
॰ Skipping a poison base left THREE, now base kind १ (an integer), at
॰ `वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश ॱ दैर्घ्य` (artha:3055), `वाक्यविभागॱ…आज्ञाकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य`
॰ (encode:6730) and `सङ्केतनॱअन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः ॱ पङ्क्ति` (shrinkhala:2106) —
॰ all three CROSS-MODULE GLOBAL READS. An unresolved cross-module global types as
॰ a plain integer, which is the SAME kind a genuine `७ ॱ क्षेत्रम्` gives.
॰ THIS CHECKER CANNOT TELL THE TWO APART, so no refusal on this signal is sound
॰ in every configuration, and a refusal that fires only when a collect pass ran
॰ would be a guard whose precondition an ordinary build removes.
॰ So all four COUNT and none refuses. That still closes what the exits were:
॰ four returns of the poison that no instrument could see. `कूट` says WHICH one,
॰ since they want different repairs — १ is the program's, ४ is `घोषणासञ्चय`'s,
॰ and २/३ are this checker's own tables disagreeing.
सार्वजनिक चरः अनिर्णीतधारसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अनिर्णीतधारमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
