॰ ॥ सञ्चयसिद्धिः ॥ ASSERT THAT A COLLECTION PASS HAS RUN OVER THIS INTERPRETER.
॰ W-223 part 2, 2026-09-04. Whoever filled `घोषणासञ्चय` calls this, and only
॰ then does `सदस्यनिर्णयः` consult the store.
॰
॰ IT IS A CALL AND NOT A WRITE because the state must be ASSERTED by someone
॰ rather than inferred from a silence. The alternative — treat an empty store as
॰ "nobody collected" — cannot tell "the instrument was not run" from "the
॰ instrument ran and found nothing", which is the defect this corpus keeps
॰ finding in other costumes: a loader's empty value reporting health, a census
॰ sharing the walk of the thing it measures.
॰
॰ THERE IS NO LOWERING ROUTINE, deliberately. A caller who wants the flag down
॰ wants a fresh interpreter, and `निर्णायकारम्भः` does NOT clear it — the flag
॰ records what the CALLER did, which a new resolver does not undo.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः सञ्चयसिद्धिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् १ ।
इति

॰ ॥ सञ्चयसंज्ञा ॥ THE SYMBOL A CROSS-MODULE MEMBER IS INTERNED UNDER. W-223
॰ part 2, 2026-09-04. One symbol per store entry, minted on first use and
॰ recorded in `सञ्चयसंज्ञाकोश` so every later use of the same member answers it.
॰
॰ NOT `घोषणम्`, and that is the whole design. `घोषणम्` pushes the name into the
॰ INNERMOST scope, which would do two wrong things: a second use of the same
॰ member in one scope would meet `पुनरुक्तघोषणम्` and be refused, and the bare
॰ member name would become resolvable locally — `सङ्केतनॱदशाङ्कमूल्यम्` would put
॰ `दशाङ्कमूल्यम्` in scope. A cross-module member belongs to no scope of this
॰ program. So the symbol is minted directly, exactly as `घोषणम्` mints it, and
॰ only the arenas keyed by SymbolId are written.
॰
॰ THE RETURN TYPE IS RECORDED WHERE THE STORE'S TEXT MAPS. The store keeps a
॰ type as TEXT in the source's own spelling, by design; `मूलप्रकारार्थः` turns a
॰ PRIMITIVE spelling into an `अर्थप्रकार` and answers `दोषार्थः` for anything
॰ else, and there is no reader from a WRAPPED spelling — `अङ्कः अन्तः अ८`,
॰ `सम्भाव्य न६४` — because `प्रकारार्थः` reaches wrappers through the AST, which
॰ the store does not keep. Those are left UNRECORDED and COUNTED in
॰ `अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या`, which is `W-248`'s acceptance number. A symbol with no
॰ recorded return is still a symbol: `ir.t1` needs only that the callee HAS one,
॰ so the two qualified calls it refuses close either way, while
॰ `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः`'s call arm — which reads `संज्ञाप्रकारकोश` — closes only for
॰ the primitives until W-248 lands. Recording ० rather than a guess is the
॰ point: a wrong type would be believed.
वृत्तिः सञ्चयसंज्ञा आदाय निर्णायकः ॱॱ निर्णायक प्रविष्टिः ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य सञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        यदि सञ्चयसंज्ञाप्रविष्टयः अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः समम् प्रविष्टिः आदि
            प्रत्यागमनम् सञ्चयसंज्ञामूल्यानि अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः ।
        इति
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति

    चरः संज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति संज्ञाग्रहणम् निर्णायकः ।

    चरः प्रकारपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिप्रकारः प्रविष्टिः ।
    ॰ NOT `प्रकारः` — a FROZEN KEYWORD of spec/grammar-t1.ebnf, which
    ॰ `no_t1_source_binds_a_frozen_keyword_as_a_name` refuses. W-231 hit this in
    ॰ this same file and renamed its binding `परीक्ष्यप्रकार`; I wrote it again
    ॰ here, so the note is at the SITE this time rather than only in that row.
    ॰ `W-248`: `प्रकारपाठार्थः` and not `मूलप्रकारार्थः`. The latter answers a
    ॰ PRIMITIVE spelling and poison for the rest, which left every wrapped
    ॰ return unrecorded; the former is the primitive arm plus the four wrappers,
    ॰ recursively, and refuses what it does not know BY NAME.
    ॰ `W-265`: READ IN THE ENTRY'S OWN MODULE. The store keeps a type as TEXT in
    ॰ the source's own spelling, so a BARE `चिह्नक` in `पदविभाग`'s entry names
    ॰ `पदविभाग`'s type — the module is a fact the entry carries, and handing it
    ॰ to the reader is reading the text rather than guessing at it. Without it a
    ॰ named return could only ever be resolved against the program doing the
    ॰ resolving, which is the wrong module by construction.
    ॰
    ॰ AND AN ENTRY WITH NO TYPE TEXT IS NOT AN UNRECORDED RETURN. A `संरचना`, a
    ॰ `गणना` and a `वृत्ति` with no `ददाति` declare no type at all; counting them
    ॰ in `अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या` made one number out of "the reader could not read
    ॰ this return" and "there is no return here". They are counted apart and the
    ॰ two still sum to what the one used to hold.
    चरः प्रविष्टिमण्डलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिमण्डलम् प्रविष्टिः ।
    चरः प्रकारसूचकः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    यदि प्रकारपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
        रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या भवति रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या योगः १ ।
    इति अन्यथा आदि
        चरः सञ्चितप्रकार ॱॱ अर्थप्रकार भवति मण्डलप्रकारपाठार्थः प्रकारपाठ प्रविष्टिमण्डलम् ।
        यदि सञ्चितप्रकार ॱ भेद असमम् दोषार्थभेद आदि
            प्रकारसूचकः भवति अर्थप्रकारयोजनम् सञ्चितप्रकार ।
        इति अन्यथा आदि
            अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या भवति अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या योगः १ ।
        इति
    इति

    ॰ ॥ BOTH MINTERS WRITE ALL THREE ARENAS — AN INVARIANT, NOT A COINCIDENCE ॥
    ॰ 2026-09-04, under `W-245`'s amendment.
    ॰
    ॰ `संज्ञाग्रहणम्` has TWO callers. `घोषणम्` writes the type, the kind and the
    ॰ declaration at one index. THIS ROUTINE WROTE ONLY THE TYPE, so every
    ॰ cross-module member interned here advanced the counter and filled one arena
    ॰ of three; the next `घोषणम्` wrote at a HIGHER index, and `nirvahana.rs:1364`
    ॰ padded the slots between with `Value::Nil` — holes INSIDE the length, which a
    ॰ length guard passes and `असमम् ०` reads as "written".
    ॰
    ॰ MEASURED before this was written: resolving `encode.t1` against the collected
    ॰ store left TWENTY holes above the reserved slot in each of `संज्ञाभेदकोश` and
    ॰ `संज्ञाघोषणाकोश`, at symbols २१९, २३१, ४१८, ४४४, ४६७, ४६८, ४६९, ५५२ and the
    ॰ rest. AFTER: one hole in each, at index ०, which is the reserved slot every
    ॰ arena in this corpus leaves unwritten and is not a hole at all.
    ॰
    ॰ ॥ THE SYMPTOM YOU REPAIR TELLS YOU NOTHING ABOUT HOW MANY THE CAUSE HAS ॥
    ॰ Those twenty symbols are the SAME TWENTY that surfaced hours earlier, in
    ॰ `W-253`, as labels no object exported — `सङ्केतनसंज्ञा२१९`, `सङ्केतनसंज्ञा२३१`,
    ॰ `सङ्केतनसंज्ञा४१८`, `सङ्केतनसंज्ञा४६९` and the rest. There the fix was to name a
    ॰ cross-module label from the callee NODE rather than from a SymbolId that
    ॰ means nothing outside the program that minted it. That repair was correct and
    ॰ complete for what it addressed, and it revealed NOTHING about this: one
    ॰ cause — a minter that advances the counter and fills one arena of three —
    ॰ presenting as an unresolvable label in the linker and as an unwritten kind in
    ॰ the IR, hours apart, in different crates, looking unrelated. Neither symptom
    ॰ points at the other. Only counting the holes did.
    ॰
    ॰ THE KIND IS KNOWN AND IS NOT A PLACEHOLDER. `घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिभेदः` answers
    ॰ what the member IS, and the entry is already in hand above for its type. This
    ॰ matters beyond the hole: `ir.t1`'s name arm emits a zero-argument CALL only
    ॰ when the symbol's kind is `व्याकरॱवृत्तिघोषणाभेद`, so with the kind absent every
    ॰ cross-module name fell to the Identifier stub.
    ॰
    ॰ THE DECLARATION IS ० AND THAT IS HONEST, not a second omission: a member of
    ॰ another module has NO declaration in THIS program's `व्याकरॱघोषणाकोश`, and ०
    ॰ is that arena's own sentinel for "none". It is written deliberately so the
    ॰ slot is filled rather than left for the padder.
    संज्ञाप्रकारकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य संज्ञा योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः भवति प्रकारसूचकः ।
    संज्ञाभेदकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य संज्ञा योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिभेदः प्रविष्टिः ।
    संज्ञाघोषणाकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य संज्ञा योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः भवति ० ।
    सञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति सञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क योगः १ ।
    सञ्चयसंज्ञाप्रविष्टयः अङ्कः सञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति प्रविष्टिः ।
    सञ्चयसंज्ञामूल्यानि अङ्कः सञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति आरभ्य संज्ञा योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य संज्ञा योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ सञ्चयप्रकारबन्धः ॥ GIVE EVERY TYPE THE STORE DECLARES A SYMBOL, under this
॰ resolver. `W-265`, 2026-09-05. Answers how many it bound.
॰
॰ THE STORE IS THE AUTHORITY FOR A TYPE NAME and the resolver is the authority
॰ for a symbol, so this is the one routine that needs both. A named type is
॰ reached by two roads — an AST node in the program being resolved, and a text
॰ in a store entry belonging to some other module — and only a table filled from
॰ the store can answer the second at all: `प्रकारपाठार्थः` sees a spelling and
॰ has no program.
॰
॰ IT MINTS THROUGH `सञ्चयसंज्ञा` AND NOT ITSELF. That routine's margin records
॰ what a third minter costs: `संज्ञाग्रहणम्` has two callers and BOTH must write
॰ all three symbol-keyed arenas or `nirvahana.rs:1364` pads the gap with `Nil` —
॰ holes INSIDE the length, which a length guard passes. Reusing it also makes a
॰ type interned here and a member interned there answer the SAME symbol for the
॰ same entry, which is what its cache is for.
॰
॰ THE EMPTY-TEXT COUNTER IS RESTORED, deliberately. A type DECLARATION carries
॰ no type text, so every entry this walks takes `सञ्चयसंज्ञा`'s empty branch;
॰ letting those land in `रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या` would make that number count
॰ this pass's own traffic rather than the corpus's. The counter measures what
॰ RESOLUTION met, and this runs before resolution begins.
॰
॰ GUARDED BY `सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति` for the reason `सदस्यनिर्णयः` states: the store
॰ may not be in the image at all, and under a lowered flag nothing here is
॰ called, so it need not be.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः सञ्चयप्रकारबन्धः आदाय निर्णायकः ॱॱ निर्णायक ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति

    चरः रिक्तपूर्वम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या ।
    ॰ NOT `गणना` — the frozen enum keyword; see `प्रकारसंज्ञासंख्या` above.
    चरः परिगणना ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        चरः प्रविष्टिभेदः ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिभेदः क्रमः ।
        चरः अर्थभेदः ॱॱ न६४ भवति प्रकारघोषणार्थभेदः प्रविष्टिभेदः ।
        यदि अर्थभेदः अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः प्रकारनाम ॱॱ पाठ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिनाम क्रमः ।
            चरः प्रकारमण्डलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिमण्डलम् क्रमः ।
            ॰ ONE BINDING PER (spelling, module). A module declaring the same
            ॰ type name twice is `W-247`'s defect and belongs to whoever resolves
            ॰ that module, not here; binding it twice would make
            ॰ `प्रकारसंज्ञासंख्या` read २ and turn one module's duplicate into an
            ॰ AMBIGUITY refusal for every reader of that spelling.
            चरः पूर्वस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति प्रकारसंज्ञान्वेषणम् प्रकारनाम प्रकारमण्डलम् ।
            यदि पूर्वस्थलम् समम् ० आदि
                चरः प्रकारसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति सञ्चयसंज्ञा निर्णायकः क्रमः ।
                प्रकारसंज्ञायोजनम् प्रकारनाम प्रकारमण्डलम् अर्थभेदः प्रकारसंज्ञा ।
                परिगणना भवति परिगणना योगः १ ।
            इति
        इति
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति

    रिक्तसञ्चितप्रकारसंख्या भवति रिक्तपूर्वम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् परिगणना ।
इति

॰ ॥ सदस्यनिर्णयः ॥ RESOLVE ONE QUALIFIED USE AGAINST THE STORE, answering the
॰ SymbolId+१ to write on the node, or ० when the member is taken on trust.
॰ W-223 part 2. The refusal is recorded in `असदस्यमस्ति`; a caller tests that
॰ before believing a ०, exactly as a reader tests `अनिर्णीतमस्ति`.
॰
॰ `निषेधशुद्धिः` FIRST, EVERY TIME. `सञ्चयदोषभेद` is STICKY — `निषेधः` sets it and
॰ only `निषेधशुद्धिः` clears it — so a lookup that did not clear would read the
॰ kind left by an EARLIER failure and take the wrong branch: a module that is
॰ merely uncollected would be reported as a module missing a member, turning a
॰ trust into a refusal on evidence belonging to another name.
॰ `V-008` PART 2 — WHETHER `<module>ॱ<member>` IS ONE OF THE FOUR VECTOR BUILT-INS
॰ (owner ruling 2026-10-05, option A). `व्यूह` is a qualifier and NOT a module: no
॰ source declares it and none can be imported, so the import check below would
॰ refuse every `व्यूहॱप्लवयोगः`. The trust is as narrow as the float built-ins':
॰ the qualifier must be exactly `व्यूह` AND the member exactly one of the four
॰ names `ir.t1`'s `व्यूहान्तर्निहितम्` lowers (`प्लवसदस्यभेदः` १..४) — any other
॰ member, and any other undeclared qualifier, still meets the import check and
॰ is refused by name. No symbol is written: like a qualified use, the node stays
॰ at ०, and `ir.t1` intercepts the call by its text before any symbol is asked.
॰ ONE TOKEN ONLY (owner ruling (B), 2026-10-05): the SPACED `व्यूह ॱ x` is always
॰ an ordinary field access — a `व्यूह` the program binds wins, and an unbound
॰ one is refused like any other undeclared name. The parser cannot see scope,
॰ so no spaced spelling can be decided as a built-in there.
॰ FORK-JOIN: the checker saw `समान्तरॱचालनम्` (the qualifier is no module, as `व्यूह` is none,
॰ and the member is the one name; `ir.t1` lowers the call by its text). Read by
॰ `ir.t1`'s pre-pass so that a program without the member pays nothing.
सार्वजनिक चरः समान्तरदृष्टम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
वृत्तिः व्यूहसदस्यः आदाय मण्डलपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ सदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति बूल आदि
    यदि मण्डलपाठ समम् उक्तम् समान्तर इति आदि
        यदि सदस्यपाठ समम् उक्तम् चालनम् इति आदि
            समान्तरदृष्टम् भवति सत्यम् ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
        इति
        प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
    इति
    यदि मण्डलपाठ असमम् उक्तम् व्यूह इति आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
    इति
    यदि सदस्यपाठ समम् उक्तम् प्लवयोगः इति आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि सदस्यपाठ समम् उक्तम् प्लववियोगः इति आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि सदस्यपाठ समम् उक्तम् प्लवगुणनम् इति आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    यदि सदस्यपाठ समम् उक्तम् प्लवभागः इति आदि प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् । इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् आव्यूहसदस्यः सदस्यपाठ ।
इति

॰ `V-009` PART (ii) — THE MATRIX MEMBERS AND THE THREE LAYOUT CONSTANTS, taken on
॰ the same narrow trust behind the same `व्यूह` qualifier (ADR-0043, owner
॰ ruling 2026-10-06): `ir.t1` intercepts the three calls by their text
॰ (`आव्यूहान्तर्निहितरचना`), reads a layout constant only as a matrix call's
॰ last argument (`प्रधानभेदः`) and refuses one anywhere else.
वृत्तिः आव्यूहसदस्यः आदाय सदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति बूल आदि
    चरः सदस्यक्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सूचीपदक्रमः आरभ्य उक्तम् आव्यूहगुणनम् व्युत्क्रमः समासः पङ्क्तिप्रधानम् स्तम्भप्रधानम् परिवर्तितम् इति ऽ सदस्यपाठ समाप्तम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् सदस्यक्रमः अधिकम् ० ।
इति

॰ `V-009` (ii) — WHICH WORD of the space-separated list `सूची` `पदम्` is, from
॰ १; ० when none. ONE LOOP in place of a compare per word (owner ruling
॰ 2026-10-06, the size reduction (1)): an inline `समम् उक्तम् … इति` cost the
॰ compiler image about २३० octets each. `ir.t1` asks this too.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः सूचीपदक्रमः आदाय सूची ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ पदम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आदिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    चरः स्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः सीमा ॱॱ न६४ भवति सूची ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
    चरः अन्तिमम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति सीमा योगः १ ।
    यावत् स्थलम् न्यूनम् अन्तिमम् आदि
        चरः विरामः ॱॱ बूल भवति सत्यम् ।
        यदि स्थलम् न्यूनम् सीमा आदि
            चरः वर्णः ॱॱ अ८ भवति सूची अङ्कः स्थलम् अन्तः ।
            यदि वर्णः असमम् ३२ आदि
                विरामः भवति असत्यम् ।
            इति
        इति
        यदि विरामः समम् सत्यम् आदि
            चरः शब्दः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱखण्डपाठः सूची आदिः स्थलम् ।
            यदि शब्दः समम् पदम् आदि
                प्रत्यागमनम् क्रमः ।
            इति
            क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
            आदिः भवति स्थलम् योगः १ ।
        इति
        स्थलम् भवति स्थलम् योगः १ ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

वृत्तिः सदस्यनिर्णयः आदाय निर्णायकः ॱॱ निर्णायक मण्डलपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ सदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ पङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    ॰ NOBODY COLLECTED — trust, and count it. The store may not even be in the
    ॰ image; under this flag it is never called, so it need not be.
    यदि सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
        असञ्चितप्रयोगसंख्या भवति असञ्चितप्रयोगसंख्या योगः १ ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति

    घोषणासञ्चयॱनिषेधशुद्धिः ।
    चरः प्रविष्टिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱसदस्यान्वेषणम् मण्डलपाठ सदस्यपाठ ।
    यदि प्रविष्टिः अधिकम् ० आदि
        सञ्चितप्रयोगसंख्या भवति सञ्चितप्रयोगसंख्या योगः १ ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् सञ्चयसंज्ञा निर्णायकः प्रविष्टिः ।
    इति

    ॰ KIND १ — this module was never collected. Trust, and count it SEPARATELY
    ॰ from "no collection ran": a test that collects three modules and resolves
    ॰ a use naming a fourth is right, and must not be refused.
    यदि घोषणासञ्चयॱसञ्चयदोषभेद समम् १ आदि
        असङ्गृहीतमण्डलसंख्या भवति असङ्गृहीतमण्डलसंख्या योगः १ ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति

    ॰ KIND २ — the module IS collected and declares no such member. THE REFUSAL
    ॰ this row was written to buy.
    यदि असदस्यमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
        असदस्यनाम भवति सदस्यपाठ ।
        असदस्यमण्डल भवति मण्डलपाठ ।
        असदस्यपङ्क्ति भवति पङ्क्ति ।
        असदस्यमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः आदाय निर्णायकः ॱॱ निर्णायक अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति दोषयुक्त बूल आदि
    ॰ THE MARGIN ABOVE UNDERCOUNTS THE ARMS, and writing to it would produce
    ॰ the very resolver it warns against. It says "Numeral, StringLiteral,
    ॰ Group and Index arms are pass-throughs; Identifier is the only arm that
    ॰ acts" — that is FIVE of EIGHT. `ast.t1:29-36` also declares क्षेत्र
    ॰ (Field), आह्वान (Call) and द्विकर्म (Binary), and all three carry CHILD
    ॰ expressions in वामसूचकाङ्क and दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क. A resolver that does not
    ॰ walk them leaves every name inside a binary operation, a call argument or
    ॰ a field access UNCHECKED — "a pass that validates nothing while reporting
    ॰ success", by a different route than the one the note was watching.
    यदि अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क समम् ० आदि
        ॰ slot ० is the one every arena reserves and never fills, and a child
        ॰ index of ० is how this AST spells "no child". Not an error.
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ `न्यूनम्` INVERTED, AND NOT `अधिकसमम्`. That word was written here first
    ॰ and the parser refused it: "expected `आदि`, found `अधिकसमम्`". It is a
    ॰ LEXICON PROPOSAL WITH NO GRAMMAR PRODUCTION — `grammar_t1.rs` lists it by
    ॰ name in `OPERATORS_THE_GRAMMAR_HAS_NO_PRODUCTION_FOR`, beside `च`, `न`,
    ॰ `वा`, `शेष` and `न्यूनसमम्`. The lexicon naming a word is not the grammar
    ॰ having it, and the frozen set is `समम् असमम् न्यूनम् अधिकम्` plus the
    ॰ arithmetic — anything else must be spelled out of those.
    चरः दैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
    यदि अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क बृहत्समम् दैर्घ्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    चरः अङ्गम् ॱॱ वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जक भवति वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश अङ्कः अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
    चरः भेदः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति अङ्गम् ॱ भेद ।

    ॰ ── THE ONE ARM THAT ACTS ────────────────────────────────────────────
    ॰ `मूल्यसूचकाङ्क` is a TOKEN INDEX, not text — मध्य.त१ says so at
    ॰ अङ्कमूल्यम्. Blocker (c) is what made this reachable: `आयातः पदविभाग`.
    ॰ CORRECTED 2026-09-01. This note used to read "`चिह्नक ॱ पाठ` IS the
    ॰ token's own text and needs no slice — `ir.t1:299`". IT IS THE WHOLE
    ॰ SOURCE; the text is `अष्टक`..`पाठसीमा`, and `ir.t1:299` read the same
    ॰ field the same wrong way, so the precedent was mistaken too. Measured:
    ॰ `मेलनम्` never matched a keyword and nothing parsed. Use
    ॰ `पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः` —
    ॰ hands it straight to `अक्षरकोशॱसङ्ख्या`. (The `चिह्न` record in
    ॰ वाक्यविभाग DOES keep bounds into a shared source, which is why
    ॰ `encode.t1` needed `चिह्ननाम`; these are different records and reasoning
    ॰ across them by field name is how that gets got wrong.)
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱनामाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        चरः चिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः अङ्गम् ॱ मूल्यसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
        चरः नामपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः चिह्नकम् ।

        ॰ W-228 (b), 2026-09-04: THE SPACED QUALIFIER, `मण्डल ॱ नाम`. `व्याकर`
        ॰ folds it into this same node with `दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क` naming the member
        ॰ token, so both spellings reach ONE arm — this one. The module is the
        ॰ node's own text and is resolved exactly as the unspaced prefix below
        ॰ is: found, the node is accepted with no symbol written (a qualified
        ॰ use leaves the node at ०, as W-209 measured for the unspaced form);
        ॰ missing, it is the undeclared name. The member is not checked in
        ॰ either spelling; that is one gap, not two.
        यदि अङ्गम् ॱ दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः मण्डलस्थानद्वि ॱॱ सम्भाव्य न६४ भवति नामनिर्णयः निर्णायकः नामपाठ ।   ॰ नामनिर्णयः ददाति सम्भाव्य न६४
            यदि मण्डलस्थानद्वि समम् शून्यम् आदि
                यदि अनिर्णीतमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
                    अनिर्णीतनाम भवति नामपाठ ।
                    अनिर्णीतपङ्क्ति भवति चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
                    अनिर्णीतमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
                इति
                प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
            इति

            ॰ THE MEMBER, W-223 part 2. The module half is this node's own text
            ॰ and `दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क` names the member's token.
            चरः सदस्यचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः अङ्गम् ॱ दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
            चरः सदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः सदस्यचिह्नकम् ।
            ॰ BOUND FIRST, NEVER JUXTAPOSED. A field access in an argument
            ॰ position (`चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति`) does not read as one argument — the
            ॰ same hazard `W-231`'s field arm met, where a qualified call with a
            ॰ juxtaposed argument would not read as a condition. It costs a local.
            चरः सदस्यपङ्क्ति ॱॱ न६४ भवति चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
            चरः सदस्यसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति सदस्यनिर्णयः निर्णायकः नामपाठ सदस्यपाठ सदस्यपङ्क्ति ।
            यदि असदस्यमस्ति समम् सत्यम् आदि
                प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
            इति
            यदि सदस्यसंज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
                अङ्गम् ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति सदस्यसंज्ञा ।
                वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश अङ्कः अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति अङ्गम् ।
            इति
            प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
        इति

        ॰ A QUALIFIED NAME RESOLVES AGAINST ITS IMPORT — added 2026-09-01.
        ॰ `पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश` is ONE token (the lexer peels only a leading or
        ॰ trailing sign, so an interior `ॱ` stays inside the word), and it names
        ॰ something in ANOTHER module, which this file declares nothing of.
        ॰ Measured: 65 such uses were refused.
        ॰
        ॰ WHAT IS CHECKED IS THE IMPORT, NOT THE MARK. Accepting any name that
        ॰ merely CONTAINS a `ॱ` would resolve `कल्पितॱकिञ्चित्` from a module
        ॰ never imported — switching the check off for every qualified name in
        ॰ the corpus rather than performing it. `आयातः` is a declaration now,
        ॰ so the MODULE half is looked up exactly like any other name.
        ॰
        ॰ WHAT IS NOT CHECKED, said plainly: that the other module actually has
        ॰ this member. That needs its symbol table, which this pass does not
        ॰ load. The import is verified; the member is taken on trust.
        चरः उपसर्गः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱमण्डलउपसर्गः नामपाठ ।
        यदि उपसर्गः ॱ दैर्घ्य अधिकम् ० आदि
            ॰ NOT `मण्डलम्` — that is a FROZEN KEYWORD of the grammar, and a
            ॰ keyword "is also a possible identifier ... the reader must prefer
            ॰ the keyword", so binding it as a name is already illegal.
            ॰ `no_t1_source_binds_a_frozen_keyword_as_a_name` caught it.
            ॰ `V-008` part 2 — THE VECTOR BUILT-INS, one token: see `व्यूहसदस्यः`.
            चरः व्यूहउपसर्गदैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति उपसर्गः ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
            चरः व्यूहनामदैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति नामपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
            चरः व्यूहसदस्यादिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य व्यूहउपसर्गदैर्घ्यम् योगः ३ समाप्तम् ।
            चरः व्यूहएकसदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱखण्डपाठः नामपाठ व्यूहसदस्यादिः व्यूहनामदैर्घ्यम् ।
            यदि व्यूहसदस्यः आरभ्य उपसर्गः ऽ व्यूहएकसदस्यपाठ समाप्तम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
                प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
            इति
            चरः मण्डलस्थानम् ॱॱ सम्भाव्य अ६४ भवति नामनिर्णयः निर्णायकः उपसर्गः ।
            यदि मण्डलस्थानम् समम् शून्यम् आदि
                यदि अनिर्णीतमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
                    अनिर्णीतनाम भवति नामपाठ ।
                    अनिर्णीतपङ्क्ति भवति चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
                    अनिर्णीतमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
                इति
                प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
            इति

            ॰ THE MEMBER, W-223 part 2. One token here, so the member is the
            ॰ half AFTER the mark: `मण्डलउपसर्गः` matched `ॱ` as the byte triple
            ॰ २२४ १६५ १७७ (U+0971), so the member begins three bytes past the
            ॰ prefix. `खण्डपाठः`'s `सीमा` is an EXCLUSIVE end, not a length.
            ॰ EVERY ARGUMENT BOUND FIRST — see the spaced arm above for why.
            चरः उपसर्गदैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति उपसर्गः ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
            चरः नामदैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति नामपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
            चरः सदस्यादिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य उपसर्गदैर्घ्यम् योगः ३ समाप्तम् ।
            चरः सदस्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱखण्डपाठः नामपाठ सदस्यादिः नामदैर्घ्यम् ।
            चरः सदस्यपङ्क्तिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
            चरः सदस्यसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति सदस्यनिर्णयः निर्णायकः उपसर्गः सदस्यपाठ सदस्यपङ्क्तिः ।
            यदि असदस्यमस्ति समम् सत्यम् आदि
                प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
            इति
            यदि सदस्यसंज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
                अङ्गम् ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति सदस्यसंज्ञा ।
                वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश अङ्कः अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति अङ्गम् ।
            इति
            प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
        इति

        चरः स्थानम् ॱॱ सम्भाव्य अ६४ भवति नामनिर्णयः निर्णायकः नामपाठ ।
        यदि स्थानम् समम् शून्यम् आदि
            ॰ THE WHOLE POINT OF THE PASS. Rust: "we just need to ensure the
            ॰ pass exists and validates scoping". A program naming a variable
            ॰ nothing declared is refused here or nowhere.
            यदि अनिर्णीतमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
                अनिर्णीतनाम भवति नामपाठ ।
                अनिर्णीतपङ्क्ति भवति चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
                अनिर्णीतमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
            इति
            प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
        इति
        ॰ W-183: write the symbol back onto the node (+१, ० = unresolved), copy-modify-write.
        अङ्गम् ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति आरभ्य स्थानम् योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
        वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश अङ्कः अभिव्यञ्जकसूचकाङ्क अन्तः भवति अङ्गम् ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ ── LEAVES: nothing to resolve ───────────────────────────────────────
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱअङ्काभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱउक्ताभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ A LITERAL RESOLVES, like a numeral and a string. It names nothing, so
    ॰ there is nothing to look up and nothing to refuse.
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱबूलाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱशून्याभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ AN EMBED`S TABLE IS NOT A PROGRAM NAME, and this arm said it was.
    ॰
    ॰ CORRECTED 2026-09-01 BY THE CORPUS. The first version resolved
    ॰ `मूल्यसूचकाङ्क` through `नामनिर्णयः` "exactly as a bare name`s", and its
    ॰ test asserted that an embed of an undeclared table must be REFUSED. Both
    ॰ were wrong about the NAMESPACE. Measured: with the arm in place,
    ॰ `samyojana.t1` stopped refusing `समावेशः` and began refusing
    ॰ `संस्कारकोशः`, and `sanskrit_text.t1` `शिवसूत्रकोशः` -- the table names
    ॰ themselves. They are not declared in the program and never will be.
    ॰
    ॰ A TABLE LIVES IN A REGISTRY, NOT IN A SCOPE. `anita::table_path` holds the
    ॰ list and `anita::resolve` REFUSES an unknown one at load time -- "`X` is
    ॰ not a table this program may bring in" -- before this pass ever runs. So
    ॰ the check exists, it is simply not this pass`s, and duplicating it here
    ॰ against the wrong namespace turns every valid embed into an error.
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱसमावेशाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ A NEGATION RESOLVES ITS OPERAND — the fallthrough below would do it, but
    ॰ only after resolving `दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क` too, which a unary node does not
    ॰ have. `०` there means NO CHILD and answers सत्यम्, so the fallthrough
    ॰ would work; this arm says the shape out loud instead of relying on it.
    यदि भेदः समम् वास्तुॱऋणाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः निर्णायकः अङ्गम् ॱ वामसूचकाङ्क ।
    इति

    ॰ ── EVERY OTHER KIND CARRIES CHILDREN, so walk both. Group and Index
    ॰ were called pass-throughs; Group holds its inner expression and Index
    ॰ holds a base AND a subscript, so "pass through" means DESCEND, not stop.
    चरः वामः ॱॱ बूल भवति अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः निर्णायकः अङ्गम् ॱ वामसूचकाङ्क ।
    यदि वामः समम् असत्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः निर्णायकः अङ्गम् ॱ दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क ।
इति

॰ the line a statement begins on, ० when it has no token — `W-240`.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः वाक्यपङ्क्तिः आदाय वाक्यसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि वाक्यसूचकाङ्क समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    यदि वास्तुॱवाक्यकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य न्यूनम् आरभ्य वाक्यसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    चरः वाक्यम् ॱॱ वास्तुॱवाक्य भवति वास्तुॱवाक्यकोश अङ्कः वाक्यसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
    चरः चिह्नकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यम् ॱ स्थानसूचकाङ्क ।
    यदि चिह्नकाङ्क समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    यदि चिह्नकाङ्क अधिकम् पदविभागॱचिह्नकसूचकाङ्क आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    चरः चिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः चिह्नकाङ्क अन्तः ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् चिह्नकम् ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
इति

॰ a type checker borrowing a finished resolver — TypeChecker::new.
॰ IT RETURNS THE RESOLVER AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF IT, which is a claim
॰ worth defending rather than a shortcut. Rust's TypeChecker has three
॰ fields: `resolver`, which is the borrow, and `types` and `node_types`,
॰ which are `HashMap::new()` in the constructor and are NEVER INSERTED INTO
॰ anywhere in typecheck.rs — the same state `resolved_symbols` is in, and
॰ the same reason निर्णायक does not mirror it. Two empty maps nothing writes
॰ and nothing reads are not structure; giving them a संरचना here would make
॰ this port claim a capability the original does not have.
॰ ॥ अप्रकार्यशर्तसंख्या ॥ CONDITIONS THE CHECKER COULD NOT TYPE. W-202.
॰
॰ NOT A COUNT OF BAD PROGRAMS — a count of what THIS PASS cannot yet see, and
॰ the difference is the whole reason it exists rather than a refusal.
॰
॰ `यदि` and `यावत्` require a बूल condition. When the condition types to a REAL
॰ type that is not बूल — `यदि स योगः १`, which types अ३२ — that is a judgement
॰ the checker can make and it refuses. When the condition types to दोषार्थः the
॰ checker does not know WHAT it is, and refusing would report the corpus for
॰ the typer's own gaps: `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः` has no arm for a call, for
॰ क्षेत्राभिव्यञ्जक, for `शून्यम्` or for समावेश, so `यदि संज्ञावाहकार्थः वामः ॱ
॰ भेद आदि` is poison even though `संज्ञावाहकार्थः` is declared `ददाति बूल` and
॰ the test is perfectly well formed.
॰
॰ MEASURED: refusing those took the typecheck census from 15 of 15 to 6, and
॰ ALL EIGHT refusals were this — not one was a defect. Counting them instead
॰ keeps the rule's teeth exactly where the typer can see, and makes the blind
॰ spot a NUMBER rather than eight verdicts that read like corpus defects.
॰ `W-231` drives this to zero by giving those kinds arms; this is its
॰ acceptance number.
सार्वजनिक चरः अप्रकार्यशर्तसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ अप्रकार्यवाक्यसंख्या ॥ EXPRESSION STATEMENTS THE CHECKER COULD NOT TYPE.
॰ W-202, and the sibling of the counter above.
॰
॰ THE FOLD POISONS ON A CHILD THAT REFUSED, AND MUST NOT ON ONE THAT SAID
॰ NOTHING. A `यदि`, a `यावत्` or a nested block answering दोषार्थः made a
॰ JUDGEMENT — its condition typed to a real non-बूल type, or something inside it
॰ did — and a refusal must not be swallowed by a well-typed statement after it.
॰ An EXPRESSION STATEMENT answering दोषार्थः made no judgement at all: its value
॰ is DISCARDED by definition, evaluated for effect, so whether this pass can
॰ type it changes nothing about the block that holds it.
॰
॰ In the paradigm a non-tail expression statement is a MARKER: its value is
॰ withheld, and only a value that is READ can judge.
॰
॰ MEASURED: bare calls in statement position — `चिह्नकयोजनम् भेद मूल पदारम्भः
॰ शिरोन्तः अक्षरसूचकाङ्क पङ्क्ति ।` at `पदविभाग.त१`'s `पदविभाग` is one — poisoned
॰ six of fifteen sources, every one a well-formed call whose value nobody wanted.
॰ `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः` has no arm for a call, so it answers दोषार्थः and the whole
॰ routine was refused for it.
॰
॰ THE LAST CHILD IS NOT EXEMPT and needs no special case: its type IS the
॰ block's answer, so a TAIL call still carries its दोषार्थः out and still refuses
॰ against a declared return. Only the poisoning of its siblings is withheld.
सार्वजनिक चरः अप्रकार्यवाक्यसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ THE FIRST STATEMENT THAT POISONED A BLOCK ॥ W-231's proof.
॰
॰ The census reports a refused FILE and the routine it refused in, and that is
॰ where the trail ended: `W-231` could say the typecheck refusals were "field
॰ accesses, probably" and could not say WHICH statement. A reading is not a
॰ measurement, and this row was asked for the measurement.
॰
॰ THE FIRST, NOT THE LAST, for the reason `अनिर्णीतनाम` records: every later
॰ poison overwrote the earlier one and the record named where the walk ENDED
॰ rather than where it first went wrong. `प्रकारपरीक्षकारम्भः` clears the guard.
सार्वजनिक चरः दुष्टवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ MERGE 2026-09-04 (trunk, W-231 onto W-240): `वास्तुॱवाक्य ॱ स्थान` — an octet run the parser never
॰ wrote — became `स्थानसूचकाङ्क`, the statement's first token (W-240); the instrument's location is
॰ that token index now, a न६४, not a run.
सार्वजनिक चरः दुष्टवाक्यस्थान ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः दुष्टवाक्यमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।

॰ WHY it poisoned, which is what a reader can act on. `वाक्ययोजनम्` takes only
॰ (भेद, वाम, दक्षिण) and NEVER SETS `स्थान`, so a statement cannot be named by
॰ line — the record has the field and the parser never fills it, the same gap
॰ `अनिर्णीतपङ्क्ति` closed for names and still open for statements. A REASON is
॰ better than an index anyway: it says which rule refused and therefore which
॰ row closes it.
॰   १ a `यदि`/`यावत्` condition that types to a REAL non-बूल type
॰   २ a `यदि` whose two branches do not meet
॰   ३ a `यावत्` whose body poisoned
॰   ४ an INDEXED WRITE whose base is a REAL type that is not a run
सार्वजनिक चरः दुष्टकारण ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ असूचीलक्ष्यसंख्या ॥ INDEXED WRITES REFUSED BECAUSE THE BASE IS NOT A RUN.
॰
॰ THE HOLE THIS COUNTS WAS OPEN UNTIL 2026-09-28 AND IT WAS A WRITE PRIMITIVE.
॰ `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः` has typed an index EXPRESSION correctly since W-202 — a
॰ non-run base answers दोषार्थः at `:1207`-`:1216` — and the assignment arm
॰ computed its target's type into `लक्ष्यार्थः` AND NEVER READ IT. So
॰ `पिटकम् ॱ शब्दः अङ्कः ० अन्तः भवति ६५ ।` on a plain `अ६४` compiled, and
॰ `ir.t1` lowered it to `निधानम्` at `[the word's VALUE + ०]`: the declared
॰ integer was taken as an ADDRESS, with no bound and no type behind it. A
॰ program could store any octet at any address by naming a number.
॰
॰ THE READ RULE DID NOT COVER THE WRITE and I concluded twice that it did —
॰ `e959aab5`, retracted by `3a07d492`. A rule that types a READ says nothing
॰ about a WRITE target; they are different paths in this same routine.
सार्वजनिक चरः असूचीलक्ष्यसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ अप्रकार्यलक्ष्यसंख्या ॥ THE BLIND SPOT BESIDE IT, AND WHY IT IS SEPARATE.
॰
॰ A base that types to दोषार्थः has made NO judgement — this pass has no arm
॰ for its shape — so refusing on it would refuse every indexed write through a
॰ call or any other untyped base, and break the corpus. That is exactly the
॰ distinction `अप्रकार्यशर्तसंख्या` draws for conditions: poison is COUNTED,
॰ a real wrong type is REFUSED. This number is the acceptance figure for
॰ closing the remaining arms; it is not a defect count.
सार्वजनिक चरः अप्रकार्यलक्ष्यसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ॥ IS THIS STATEMENT'S VALUE READ? ॥ W-231's tail-position refinement.
॰
॰ `W-202` exempted a non-tail EXPRESSION statement from poisoning its block
॰ because its value is discarded — "only a value that is READ can judge" — and
॰ left conditionals poisoning on the grounds that a conditional DID judge. It
॰ judges its CONDITION. It does not judge the agreement of two branch values
॰ that are about to be thrown away, and a `यदि` mid-body is in exactly the
॰ position an expression statement is.
॰
॰ MEASURED before the change: FOUR of the five refusing sources refused on the
॰ join, every one of them a conditional whose value nobody reads.
॰
॰ So the join applies where the conditional's value IS the block's — the LAST
॰ child, read at the bottom of the समूह arm — and mid-body a disagreement is
॰ COUNTED (`अयुग्मशाखासंख्या`). The CONDITION rule is untouched and applies in
॰ every position: a test that is not a judgement is wrong wherever it sits.
सार्वजनिक चरः पुच्छे ॱॱ बूल भवति सत्यम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अयुग्मशाखासंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ Conditions that type to a REAL non-बूल type — refused in every position, and
॰ counted so the corpus can say whether that is ONE site (a defect in a source)
॰ or a PATTERN (integers used as truth, which is the owner's grammar decision:
॰ a consonant is an operation, so implicit truthiness would be a silent one).
सार्वजनिक चरः अबूलशर्तसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः प्रकारपरीक्षकारम्भः आदाय निर्णायकः ॱॱ निर्णायक ददाति निर्णायक आदि
    अप्रकार्यशर्तसंख्या भवति ० ।
    अप्रकार्यवाक्यसंख्या भवति ० ।
    अप्रकार्यवाक्यमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    अप्रकार्यवाक्यस्थान भवति ० ।
    दुष्टवाक्यमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    दुष्टवाक्यभेद भवति ० ।
    दुष्टकारण भवति ० ।
    अयुग्मशाखासंख्या भवति ० ।
    अबूलशर्तसंख्या भवति ० ।
    ॰ ZEROED HERE OR THE CENSUS SUMS CUMULATIVELY: this pass shares one
    ॰ interpreter across the corpus, and the margin at the census's call to this
    ॰ routine records what that cost the last time a counter did not restart
    ॰ while the thing it counts did — `unjoined_branches` 337 against a true 53.
    ॰ THE TWO TEXTS ARE LEFT STANDING, for the reason the margin at
    ॰ `कार्यक्रमप्रकारपरीक्षा` gives for `प्रकारदोषनाम`: `भवति ०` is
    ॰ type-directed in a DECLARATION, where it means the empty run, but here it
    ॰ is an ASSIGNMENT and would put `Int(0)` into a slice-typed global. A
    ॰ reader tests the bool before reading either name.
    असत्क्षेत्रसंख्या भवति ० ।
    असत्क्षेत्रमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    असत्क्षेत्रपङ्क्ति भवति ० ।
    असञ्चितक्षेत्रसंख्या भवति ० ।
    असञ्चितक्षेत्रमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    असञ्चितक्षेत्रपङ्क्ति भवति ० ।
    अऋण्यसंख्या भवति ० ।
    अनिर्णीतधारसंख्या भवति ० ।
    अनिर्णीतधारमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    अनिर्णीतधारपङ्क्ति भवति ० ।
    अऋण्यमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    अऋण्यभेद भवति ० ।
    ॰ `W-359`: the count and the bool; the name is left standing (see above).
    वर्धनबन्धदोषसंख्या भवति ० ।
    वर्धनबन्धदोषमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    वर्धनबन्धदोषभेद भवति ० ।
    वर्धनबन्धदोषपङ्क्ति भवति ० ।
    पुच्छे भवति सत्यम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् निर्णायकः ।
इति

॰ typecheck every declaration of a program — typecheck_program.
॰ ALL THREE OF ITS PARTS NOW EXIST: प्रत्यागमनसाम्यम् is its one rule,
॰ वाक्यप्रकारः below types the body, and प्रकारार्थः would give the declared
॰ return type. What it cannot do is find the declarations to apply them to —
॰ see (b) — and its return type would come from प्रकारार्थः, which is (c)
॰ and (d). It is the last routine of this file to unblock, not the first.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः कार्यक्रमप्रकारपरीक्षा आदाय कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति दोषयुक्त बूल आदि
    ॰ ALL THREE PARTS EXIST NOW, and the note above said so: `प्रत्यागमनसाम्यम्`
    ॰ is its one rule, `वाक्यप्रकारः` types the body, and `प्रकारार्थः` gives
    ॰ the declared return type. What it could not do was FIND the declarations
    ॰ — (b) — and that reduced to `आयातः व्याकर`, taken at the head of this file.
    ॰
    ॰ THE BOUND IS THE ARENA'S OWN दैर्घ्य, and slot ० is read, for
    ॰ `कार्यक्रमनिर्णयः`'s reason: `व्याकर`'s declaration pushers were
    ॰ write-first until W-163 straightened them, and walking the length while
    ॰ skipping `शून्यम्` is correct under either convention.
    ॰ a fresh check has no refusal yet. ONLY THE BOOL IS CLEARED, never
    ॰ `प्रकारदोषनाम`: `भवति ०` is type-directed in a DECLARATION, where it
    ॰ means the empty run, but this is an ASSIGNMENT and would put `Int(0)`
    ॰ into a slice-typed global. The resolver's `निर्णायकारम्भः` clears its
    ॰ bool and leaves its name for the same reason; a reader tests the bool
    ॰ before reading the name.
    प्रकारदोषमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    प्रकारदोषपङ्क्ति भवति ० ।

    ॰ THE RANGE, as `कार्यक्रमनिर्णयः` above takes it and for the same reason —
